{
  "description": "\"Visibility decides which binding an assignment reaches, never statement order\" (spec/execution-model.md:483-490), pinned with both touch orders against ONE global and interleaved: `bump` reads before it writes, `reset` only ever writes, and the program prints `2`, `0`, `1`. Each of the three reads a different way the write could go wrong — `2` that `bump`'s read-first writes accumulate across calls, `0` that `reset`'s write-only touch reached the same binding rather than a discarded procedure-local, and `1` that the global is still shared and writable AFTER a write-only procedure has touched it. Measured: under an unqualified \"an assignment inside a procedure creates a local\" rule the program prints `0`, `0`, `0` — every one of the three collapses at once, which is why the three values are asserted rather than the final one.",
